WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.139 --> 00:00:02.889
(dramatic music)

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.710
- [Narrator] One thing that
quickly becomes apparent

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.530
during the first season of "The Witcher"

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.376
is that Nilfgaard seems bad.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.626
- We're losing!

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.330
- [Narrator] We see the
armies of the Nilfgaard empire

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.870
burn Cintra and slaughter its citizens,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.390
its mages engaged in dark rituals,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.510
and its agents, especially
the sinister Cahir,

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.043
pursing Ciri ruthlessly, even going so far

00:00:27.043 --> 00:00:29.070
as to employ a doppler.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.459
- Do you not have errand
boys where you come from?

00:00:31.459 --> 00:00:34.723
- They lacked your valuable set of skills.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.390
- [Narrator] So what's up with Nilfgaard?

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.128
Are they as bad as they appear
or is there more to this

00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:43.530
still rather mysterious
empire that we're not seeing?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.900
The answer is, of course, a bit of both.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.790
The world of "The Witcher"
is a morally complex place

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.676
where there are two sides
to almost every story

00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:52.610
and absolutes are rare,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.810
even when it comes to
burning and torturing.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.840
So what do we know about Nilfgaard?

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.310
Nilfgaard is a vast empire in
the south of the continent,

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.955
the large land mass on which the stories

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:05.770
of "The Witcher" unfold.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.492
- Cintra is indeed the jewel of the north,

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:12.170
yet Nilfgaard remains
the shit rag of the south

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.596
and that's saying something.

00:01:13.596 --> 00:01:15.790
(laughing)

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:16.890
- [Narrator] In the original books

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.900
and so far in the show too,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.390
most of these stories
take place in the north,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.127
among the fragile alliances
and fractious intrigue

00:01:24.127 --> 00:01:26.590
of various competing kingdoms,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.965
like Temeria, ruled by King Foltest,

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:31.764
Redania, and Aedirn,
where we see Yennefer sent

00:01:31.764 --> 00:01:34.220
following her training at Aretuza.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.960
- What sort of a king refuses a dance

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.620
with one of his subjects?

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.580
- [Narrator] So while there's
a little more to learn

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.280
about Nilfgaard from the books,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.690
even there they're seen as outsiders.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.270
They are the invading force

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.200
and we see events from the perspective

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.660
of the invaded, as when Jaskier describes

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.671
the coming war before the fall of Cintra

00:01:51.671 --> 00:01:54.397
in the short story "Something More".

00:01:54.397 --> 00:01:57.357
"There's never been a war like
this," the bard said gravely.

00:01:57.357 --> 00:01:59.797
"The Nilfgaard army are
leaving scorched earth

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:00.947
"and bodies behind them.

00:02:00.947 --> 00:02:02.847
"Entire fields of corpses.

00:02:02.847 --> 00:02:06.103
"This is a war of destruction,
total destruction.

00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:08.680
"Nilfgaard against everyone."

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.632
This kind of reaction
is common in the books.

00:02:10.632 --> 00:02:12.710
A traveling priest in "The Blood of Elves"

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:14.921
warns a crowd of northerners to remember

00:02:14.921 --> 00:02:18.390
the Nilfgaard are our
punishment from the gods.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.700
They are the whip with which

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.080
the immortals will lash you sinners.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.771
And they're sometimes referred
to as the Black Forces,

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:27.380
a forbidding name which
is only partly a reference

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.210
to their dark armor.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.629
Behind these scare stories, though,

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:33.880
is perhaps a more mundane
political reality.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.430
In "Blood of Elves", Geralt's
fellow witcher Lambert

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.560
reacts to the Nilfgaardian invasion

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.407
and the history of
trouble between the empire

00:02:40.407 --> 00:02:42.987
and the northern kingdoms more casually.

00:02:42.987 --> 00:02:44.457
"So what?" said Lambert.

00:02:44.457 --> 00:02:45.337
"They've been hitting,

00:02:45.337 --> 00:02:47.364
"killing, and striking
against each other constantly

00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:49.287
"for hundreds of years.

00:02:49.287 --> 00:02:51.150
"It's nothing to worry about."

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.643
Also remember that in episode
three of "The Witcher",

00:02:53.643 --> 00:02:55.765
the Brotherhood of
Sorcerers are more concerned

00:02:55.765 --> 00:02:58.836
with reining in the
unruly kingdom of Cintra

00:02:58.836 --> 00:03:01.840
than they are with the
slumbering power of Nilfgaard

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.503
which at this time is still
ruled by somebody called Fergus.

00:03:05.503 --> 00:03:07.119
- How fares Nilfgaard?

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.628
- King Fergus is proving
to be an effective

00:03:09.628 --> 00:03:12.420
and excitable young king.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.710
- Horny she means.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.410
Spending the kingdom's money on women

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.360
as his people starve to death.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.540
- [Narrator] The truth about Nilfgaard

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.430
probably lies somewhere in the middle.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.546
Andrzej Sapkowski based
the expansionist empire

00:03:22.546 --> 00:03:25.171
on the Romans and perhaps, some
commentators have suggested,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.910
also the Soviet Russians.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.740
Nilfgaard grows through conquest,

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.910
turning vanquished enemies into provinces

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.092
and vassal states.

00:03:33.092 --> 00:03:34.505
The climatic battle at Sodden

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:36.715
was just the end of a longer campaign

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:40.339
during which the Nilfgaard
had advanced across your lands

00:03:40.339 --> 00:03:43.378
like an iron roller,
strewing the land between

00:03:43.378 --> 00:03:46.130
Marnadal and Transriver with the corpses

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.060
of many a gallant fellow.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.700
While their armies might be ruthless,

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.430
there's plenty of evidence in the books

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.750
that Nilfgaard's enemies
can be just as cruel

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.666
given the opportunity, and perhaps because

00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:58.048
of the Empire's early
connection with the elder folk,

00:03:58.048 --> 00:04:01.255
Nilfgaard has a more accepting
approach to non-humans,

00:04:01.255 --> 00:04:03.930
especially elves, when
compared to their neighbors

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:04.997
from the north.

00:04:04.997 --> 00:04:07.424
- My elders worked with humans

00:04:07.424 --> 00:04:10.430
and got robbed of all they had.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.070
- So they might not be evil,

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.460
or at least no more evil than anyone else,

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.506
but that doesn't explain why Nilfgaard

00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:18.786
invaded Cintra in the first place.

00:04:18.786 --> 00:04:20.793
What changed between the time of Fergus

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.120
and that relaxed meeting
of the Brotherhood

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.830
to the burning of Cintra

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.810
and the slaughter of its people?

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.549
The reason has been hinted at in the show

00:04:28.549 --> 00:04:30.833
through prophecy and mysterious language

00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:32.990
and particularly in this scene

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.428
where Nilfgaard mage Fringilla
reminds a downcast Cahir

00:04:36.428 --> 00:04:38.860
about the importance of their mission.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.833
- You rose up against the usurper.

00:04:43.174 --> 00:04:45.893
Helped free our people from their chains.

00:04:48.096 --> 00:04:50.423
I witnessed the white flame call on you,

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.643
mold you, anoint you.

00:05:00.463 --> 00:05:02.380
It burns in you, Cahir.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.763
She is the key,

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.333
but you, you are the commissioner.

00:05:13.499 --> 00:05:15.420
Do not despair.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.470
We will find her and we
will spread your supremacy

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.733
all through the kingdoms
whether they deserve it or not.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.200
- [Narrator] The events
and meanings behind

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.044
this moment will likely
form the foundations

00:05:27.044 --> 00:05:29.860
of the story as the show continues.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.467
So, in other words, you'll have to wait.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:35.550
"The Witcher" is available to
watch on Netflix right now.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.960
For more on "The Witcher",
other Netflix originals,

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.329
and loads more, subscribe to the channel.

00:05:40.329 --> 00:05:43.079
(dramatic music)

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.620
- The time of the sword
and the ax is nigh.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.373
(dramatic music)

